## Q23
Figure out which **non-parametric** test to run to get the correct p-value for this set of hypotheses:

$$
H_0 = \text{Each educational attainment is a sample from the same distribution of music diversity scores}
\\
H_a = \text{At least one educational attainment has stochastically higher or lower music diversity scores}
$$

I'm pretty sure it needs to be an ANOVA test.
```{r}
myAov <- aov(Music_diversity_score ~ Education, data = adults)
summary(myAov)

#ANSWER: p-value = 0.0415
```

